{"path":"experimental/ranges/iterator/dangling","title":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling, std::experimental::ranges::safe_iterator_t","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>dangling, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>safe_iterator_t","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/iterator/dangling","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The class template dangling is a simple wrapper around an object to indicate that the wrapped object may be dangling, that is, it refers to another object whose lifetime may have ended.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/ranges/iterator\">&lt;experimental/ranges/iterator&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> CopyConstructible T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> dangling <span class=\"br0\">{</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">public</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; dangling<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> requires DefaultConstructible<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; dangling<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; T get_unsafe<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> Range R <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">using</span> safe_iterator_t <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/conditional\"><span class=\"kw639\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conditional_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_lvalue_reference\"><span class=\"kw471\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_lvalue_reference</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2907\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/dangling/dangling\" data-external=\"1\"><span class=\"kw2871\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">dangling</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2907\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The class template <code>dangling</code> is a simple wrapper around an object to indicate that the wrapped object may be <i>dangling</i>, that is, it refers to another object whose lifetime may have ended.\n</p><p>The alias template <code>safe_iterator_t</code> returns the iterator type of <code>R</code>, wrapped in <code>dangling</code> if the range was an rvalue range (as indicated by <code>R</code> not being an lvalue reference type).\n</p><p>They are used by range algorithms that accept rvalue ranges and return iterators into them.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-member\">\n<h2 id=\"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::dangling\"><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::dangling::</span>dangling</h2>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dangling<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> requires DefaultConstructible<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dangling<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Default constructor. Value-initializes the wrapped object.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Initializes the wrapped object with <code>t</code>. Note that this constructor defines an implicit conversion from <code>T</code> to <code>dangling&lt;T&gt;</code>.\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"t-member\">\n<h2 id=\"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::get_unsafe\"><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::dangling::</span>get_unsafe</h2>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T get_unsafe<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a copy of the wrapped object.\n</p>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::dangling","id":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::dangling"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::get_unsafe","id":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::get_unsafe"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/ranges","title":"Extensions for ranges"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling, std::experimental::ranges::safe_iterator_t","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. The class template dangling is a simple wrapper around an object to indicate that the wrapped object may be dangling…"},{"label":"Member functions"},{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::dangling","note":"Default constructor. Value-initializes the wrapped object."},{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::dangling::get_unsafe","note":"Returns a copy of the wrapped object."}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":155,"codeBlockCount":0}
